    "However, late-February polling that narrows CDU–Greens gaps and possible district-level amplification keep a small but non-negligible tail risk, justifying a cautious contrarian notch above the baseline."
  ],
  "confidence": "low",
  "narrative": "AfD faces a steep uphill path given CDU/Greens leads and structural barriers in BW. A narrow, unlikely tail risk could emerge from late polling shifts or district-level seat amplification, but the calibrated probability remains small (around 7%).",
  "justification": {
    "anchor": {
      "probability": 0.04,
      "basis": "Reference class anchored on Baden-Württemberg state elections where AfD has not led in seat count; several polls in Feb 2026 place CDU/Greens ahead of AfD, supporting a low anchor."
    },
    "factor_updates": [
      {
        "factor": "Narrowing CDU–Greens vote-share gap in late-February polls",
